WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.383
Alert triage is the process of reviewing new events, determining priority,

00:00:04.383 --> 00:00:06.719
and deciding what action is needed.

00:00:06.719 --> 00:00:10.613
Priority should reflect potential impact, affected asset, evidence quality, urgency,

00:00:10.613 --> 00:00:14.896
and current context rather than simply repeating a vendor severity label.

00:00:14.896 --> 00:00:18.401
Confidence describes how strongly a tool supports its observation;

00:00:18.401 --> 00:00:22.295
it does not prove the event is important or correct.

00:00:22.295 --> 00:00:26.967
Show confidence with the rule, model, threshold, source quality, and relevant evidence.

00:00:26.967 --> 00:00:31.640
A high-confidence detection on an unimportant condition may still be low priority.

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:37.870
Group related events so a reviewer sees one coherent incident instead of dozens of isolated alerts.

00:00:37.870 --> 00:00:42.153
Shared assets, accounts, locations, time windows, or indicators can support grouping.

00:00:42.153 --> 00:00:45.268
Preserve individual evidence and make automated relationships explainable.

00:00:45.268 --> 00:00:49.940
False positives are alerts that incorrectly identify a problem or meaningful event.

00:00:49.940 --> 00:00:55.002
Reviewers need a clear way to mark them, record why they were wrong,

00:00:55.002 --> 00:00:58.507
and route that feedback to rule or model owners.

00:00:58.507 --> 00:01:04.347
Suppression should be narrow and time-bound so tuning does not create an unnoticed blind spot.

00:01:04.347 --> 00:01:08.630
Escalation paths should identify who handles safety, physical security, cyber, privacy,

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:09.799
or operational issues.

00:01:09.799 --> 00:01:12.524
Important actions should require appropriate human confirmation.

00:01:12.524 --> 00:01:17.197
The dashboard should not automatically make high-impact decisions about people solely from

00:01:17.197 --> 00:01:19.144
uncertain visual or behavioral inferences.

00:01:19.144 --> 00:01:22.648
Document acknowledgments, assignments, evidence reviewed, decisions, and closure reasons.

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:25.374
This creates accountability and supports later learning.

00:01:25.374 --> 00:01:30.436
A mature feedback loop uses review outcomes to improve thresholds, source quality, grouping,

00:01:30.436 --> 00:01:33.940
and playbooks while monitoring whether changes increase missed events.
